                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Bills",
                        "email": "jason.m.bills@linux.intel.com",
                        "username": "jmbills"
                    },
                    "message": "Are we confident that this will work the same as the boost code?  Perhaps an approach may be to\n1. (optional) bring back the boost header for now to fix the compile error\n2. change the `sel-delete` default to disabled so CI tests the default code path\n3. add unit tests for this parsing method testing the current boost-based code\n4. come back to this change with unit tests adding confidence that it is producing the expected results."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/sel_logger.cpp",
                    "line": 278,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Bills",
                        "email": "jason.m.bills@linux.intel.com",
                        "username": "jmbills"
                    },
                    "message": "This is the format of the SEL entry that is being parsed:\n`# \"<timestamp> <ID>,<Type>,<EventData>,[<Generator ID>,<Path>,<Direction>]\"`\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/openbmc/blob/master/meta-intel-openbmc/meta-common/recipes-extended/rsyslog/rsyslog/rsyslog.conf#L18C1-L18C76"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/sel_logger.cpp",
                    "line": 278,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "khangng-ampere",
                        "email": "khangng@os.amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "khangng-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "That is helpful, thanks"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/sel_logger.cpp",
                    "line": 278,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vernon Mauery",
                        "email": "vernon.mauery@gmail.com",
                        "username": "vmauery"
                    },
                    "message": "Could this be done more simply with a std::regex? The uniformity of the format seems like it would be a good candidate."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/sel_logger.cpp",
                    "line": 285,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Bills",
                        "email": "jason.m.bills@linux.intel.com",
                        "username": "jmbills"
                    },
                    "message": "Does this find the string ` ,` or does it find either character ' ' or ','?  It needs to split on either character."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/sel_logger.cpp",
                    "line": 285,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "khangng-ampere",
                        "email": "khangng@os.amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "khangng-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "It splits on either character, yes"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/sel_logger.cpp",
                    "line": 290,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Bills",
                        "email": "jason.m.bills@linux.intel.com",
                        "username": "jmbills"
                    },
                    "message": "The record ID should be the second field (after the timestamp)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/sel_logger.cpp",
                    "line": 290,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "khangng-ampere",
                        "email": "khangng@os.amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "khangng-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "I see, my bad. I believe that is the only bug though, but IMO bringing back the boost headers, introducing tests in this repo, then add back the change should be more preferrable."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/sel_logger.cpp",
                    "line": 290,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Bills",
                        "email": "jason.m.bills@linux.intel.com",
                        "username": "jmbills"
                    },
                    "message": "I submitted this patch to restore the boost headers: https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-sel-logger/+/84289"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/sel_logger.cpp",
                    "line": 308,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Thu Nguyen",
                        "email": "thu@os.amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "ThuBaNguyen"
                    },
                    "message": "What is 4 value? Do we have any definition for that?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/sel_logger.cpp",
                    "line": 308,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "khangng-ampere",
                        "email": "khangng@os.amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "khangng-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "> What is 4 value? Do we have any definition for that?\n\nI believe it is the number of fields for each entry. However, the goal of this patch is to just fix the compile error and keep the original behavior, so I don't want to make any false assumptions here and extract to a constant macro, just in case `4` is defined to be something else."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/sel_logger.cpp",
                    "line": 308,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "khangng-ampere",
                        "email": "khangng@os.amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "khangng-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "The `4` comes from the code replaced:\n\n```cpp\n    if (newestEntryFields.size() < 4)\n    {\n        return 0;\n    }\n```"
                }
